- **Detailed Theory:** We explore Thevenin and Norton equivalents. We discuss why a "perfect" 5V sensor might only read 4.2V when connected to a low-impedance analog input.
- **Experimental Observation:** "By measuring the Open-Circuit Voltage and the Short-Circuit Current of an analog light sensor, we derived its Thevenin resistance ($R_{th} = 4.7 k\Omega$)."
